SUMMARY:W01 • Prep — DC Lab Kit Check
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=1\n• Search this topic: https://numbercla
 w2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electricity%20Basics%20%2B%20
 Safety%20%2B%20Ohm/Watt\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alf
 red-university/labs.html\n• Assessment Center: https://numberclaw2.githu
 b.io/alfred-university/assessments.html\n• Engineering Library: https://
 numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION:
  Foundational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIO
 RITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work 
 first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHE
 CKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-001 in Practice → Lab Center → Week 01.\n2. Choos
 e your route. Virtual route: web browser only. Physical route: low-voltage
  bench supply or battery (power source)\; DMM (measure voltage/current/res
 istance)\; breadboard (solderless assembly)\; LED (load)\; 220 Ω\, 330 Ω
 \, or 1 kΩ 1/4-watt resistor (current limiting)\; jumper wires (connectio
 ns).\n3. Physical check: inspect leads and wires\, confirm the DMM fuse/le
 ads are intact\, identify LED polarity\, and keep power disconnected while
  building.\n4. If physical equipment is missing\, use the approved Falstad
  virtual route instead of stopping the course.\n5. The prep reminder is co
 mplete when you have confirmed one workable route for LAB-001.\n\nREFERENC
 E HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th 
 ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BO
 OK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrat
 aSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of th
 is event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Know what eq
 uipment/parts are required for the next practical session and what each it
 em is for.\n• Confirm every critical item is ready\, compatible\, and sa
 fe to use before the lab begins.\n• Identify any missing item early enou
 gh to obtain or substitute it without cancelling the hands-on work.\n\nCOV
 ERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover 
 every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrat
 e one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as complet
 e. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official 
 or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE
 \nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If yo
 u cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a s
 hort catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block. N
 o spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Equipment\,Embedded\,CETa
END:VEVENT
