SUMMARY:W01 • Learn — Electricity\, Safety & Ohm’s Law
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=1\n• Search this topic: https://numbercla
 w2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electricity%20Basics%20%2B%20
 Safety%20%2B%20Ohm/Watt\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Foundational ci
 rcuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core 
 → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep
  Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nSTART FROM ZERO — SESSION 1\nWHY THI
 S STARTS HERE: Every later embedded-system skill assumes you understand wh
 at voltage\, current\, resistance\, power\, ground\, polarity\, open circu
 its\, shorts\, and safe measurement mean. We are not assuming prior electr
 onics knowledge.\n\nWEEK 1 FOCUS: START FROM ZERO: Safety + What Electrici
 ty Is + Voltage / Current / Resistance + Ohm / Watt + SI Prefixes\nETA/CET
 a SCOPE — FIRST PASS: 1.1\, 1.4–1.7\, 1.10\, 1.13–1.14\; 2.1\, 2.4\,
  2.6\, 2.13–2.14\; 9.8–9.9. The narrower RF/fiber/field-safety details
  return later in CETa-specific review.\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Build the
  vocabulary and safety habits every later circuit\, instrument\, microcont
 roller\, and troubleshooting skill depends on. Set up the Git evidence not
 ebook from day one.\n\nTODAY — 8:00 PM TO 9:30 PM:\n1. Safety first (10 
 min): electrical shock basics\, de-energizing\, ESD\, and why resistance m
 easurements are made on de-energized circuits.\n2. What electricity is (15
  min): charge/electrons at a practical technician level\; do not get burie
 d in atomic physics.\n3. Learn voltage vs current vs resistance vs power (
 25 min). Explain each in your own words before moving on.\n4. Open the ETA
  Common Formulas sheet and locate Ohm's law / power relationships (5 min).
 \n5. Work 6–8 beginner Ohm/Watt problems with units (15 min). Show the r
 earrangement\; do not copy an example.\n6. Set up or confirm the GitHub la
 b notebook/repository (10 min). Create a Week_01 folder/note.\n\nMASTERY G
 ATE: In plain language\, explain charge\, voltage\, current\, resistance\,
  power\, polarity\, open vs short\, and basic ESD/shock precautions\; use 
 SI prefixes\; solve fresh Ohm/Watt problems\; then build and safely measur
 e a current-limited LED circuit on Saturday.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Learn from t
 he bottom. Watching alone never counts. Use learn → retrieve → calcula
 te/code → build/measure → debug → document. Start later study blocks
  with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. A missed session never creates an unhe
 althy make-up marathon.\n\nWEEK 1 START-FROM-ZERO RESOURCES:\n• Electric
  Current and Circuits Explained: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r-SCyD7f_
 zI\n• Electrical Safety Training: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TMT6f3
 tZQSk\n• GitHub Skills — Introduction to GitHub: https://github.com/sk
 ills/introduction-to-github\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Of
 ficial Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive 
 copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. err
 ata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE 
 — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.1 pp.1–6 SKIM only\; Ch.2 pp.7–
 14\; Ch.3 pp.16–18\; Ch.4 pp.25–26\; read the book addendum once.\nQUI
 Z / REVIEW: Ch.2 quiz p.15 after the safety lesson. Use answers p.223 only
  after finishing.\nWHY: Starts from zero with safety\, units\, Ohm/Watt an
 d the physical meaning of voltage/current/resistance before circuit analys
 is.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Curre
 nt ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older 
 book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNIN
 G OUTCOMES (WEEK 01)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to exp
 lain or demonstrate:\n• Explain voltage\, current\, resistance\, power\,
  ground/reference\, polarity\, open circuits\, and short circuits.\n• Us
 e SI prefixes and engineering notation correctly for common electronic val
 ues.\n• Apply Ohm's law and the Watt/power relationships to simple DC ci
 rcuits.\n• Recognize basic electrical hazards and use safe low-voltage m
 easurement habits.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks abo
 ve are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still can
 not explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not c
 ount that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and
  use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\
 n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learn
 ing outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, writ
 e that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next 
 available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
