 ational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: 
 CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\
 ; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nNeed by Week 3. Confirm benc
 h supply\, oscilloscope\, appropriate probes/leads\, safe low-voltage sour
 ce/circuit\, and any adapters. If you do not own an instrument yet\, recor
 d the acquisition plan\; do not improvise unsafe measurements.\n\n\nTODAY 
 — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-003 in Practice → Lab Center → Week
  03.\n2. Virtual route: web browser plus Falstad and the Tektronix virtual
 -oscilloscope resource linked in LAB-003.\n3. Physical route: DMM with lea
 ds\; adjustable low-voltage bench supply with output leads\; oscilloscope\
 ; a compatible 1×/10× probe and ground lead\; breadboard/test circuit\; 
 function generator only if available.\n4. Confirm the probe is not damaged
 \, the scope and probe ratings exceed the planned low-voltage signal\, and
  the supply starts at zero/current-limited where supported.\n5. If an inst
 rument is missing\, use the complete virtual route. Do not improvise measu
 rements on mains voltage.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Offi
 cial Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive co
 py and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errat
 a: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRE
 D LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to expl
 ain or demonstrate:\n• Know what equipment/parts are required for the ne
 xt practical session and what each item is for.\n• Confirm every critica
 l item is ready\, compatible\, and safe to use before the lab begins.\n•
  Identify any missing item early enough to obtain or substitute it without
  cancelling the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources a
 nd tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If y
 ou still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the sessio
 n\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch
 -up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closi
 ng the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then che
 ck the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an ou
 tcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it duri
 ng the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
