 %20%2B%20Voltage%20Dividers%20%2B%20DMM\n• Engineering Library: https://
 numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION:
  Foundational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIO
 RITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work 
 first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 2 FOCUS: DC Netwo
 rks + KVL/KCL + Voltage Dividers + DMM\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 4.1\; 4.10\; 4.17\
 ; 3.1.4\; 8.1–8.4\; 8.16\; 9.1–9.2\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Series/pa
 rallel networks\, voltage/current division\, meter range/connection\, LTsp
 ice prediction vs measurement.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Electronic Cir
 cuits playlist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL0o_zxa4K1BV9E-N8tS
 ExU1djL6slnjbL\n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.etai.org/Common_Formula
 s.pdf\n- LTspice: https://www.analog.com/en/resources/design-tools-and-cal
 culators/ltspice-simulator.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Solve unseen series/paral
 lel/KVL/KCLproblems\, predict test points\, then verify a built divider ne
 twork with DMM and explain any measurement error.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: watchin
 g alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code ->build/meas
 ure -> debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with~10 minutes 
 of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhea
 lthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to this we
 ek’s competencies. Create a one-page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. 
