 ur scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNME
 NT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\
 n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.3 p.19 seri
 es/parallel formulas + Ch.4 pp.27–34.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.4 quiz p.34\, t
 hen Unit 2 review p.35.\nWHY: The book's DC-circuit sequence aligns direct
 ly with series/parallel\, KVL/KCL\, voltage dividers and troubleshooting.\
 nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current E
 TA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book
  differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OU
 TCOMES (WEEK 02)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain
  or demonstrate:\n• Analyze series and parallel resistor networks.\n• 
 Use Kirchhoff's Voltage Law and Kirchhoff's Current Law to reason about ci
 rcuit behavior.\n• Design and analyze a voltage divider\, including the 
 effect of loading.\n• Predict node voltages\, branch currents\, equivale
 nt resistance\, and power.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and t
 asks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you s
 till cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, 
 do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up 
 list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing t
 he gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check t
 he learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcom
 e\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during t
 he next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
