 : Foundational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRI
 ORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work
  first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 2 FOCUS: DC Netw
 orks + KVL/KCL + Voltage Dividers + DMM\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 4.1\; 4.10\; 4.17
 \; 3.1.4\; 8.1–8.4\; 8.16\; 9.1–9.2\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Series/p
 arallel networks\, voltage/current division\, meter range/connection\, LTs
 pice prediction vs measurement.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Electronic Ci
 rcuits playlist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL0o_zxa4K1BV9E-N8t
 SExU1djL6slnjbL\n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.etai.org/Common_Formul
 as.pdf\n- LTspice: https://www.analog.com/en/resources/design-tools-and-ca
 lculators/ltspice-simulator.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Solve unseen series/para
 llel/KVL/KCLproblems\, predict test points\, then verify a built divider n
 etwork with DMM and explain any measurement error.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: watchi
 ng alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code ->build/mea
 sure -> debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with~10 minutes
  of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhe
 althy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-002 
 — Series / Parallel Network Verification in Practice → Lab Center → 
 Week 02.\n2. Choose one route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physical n
 eeds: DMM\, breadboard\, resistor assortment\, low-voltage supply.\n3. Fol
 low every numbered step under the route you selected\; predict the result 
 before simulating\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the required evidenc
 e: Schematic + calculations + predicted-vs-simulated table + troubleshooti
 ng path.\n5. Mark only the route you actually completed. A virtual complet
 ion does not claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP TH
 ESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your sca
 nned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOF
 FICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.3 p.19 series/pa
 rallel formulas + Ch.4 pp.27–34.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.4 quiz p.34\, then U
 nit 2 review p.35.\nWHY: The book's DC-circuit sequence aligns directly wi
 th series/parallel\, KVL/KCL\, voltage dividers and troubleshooting.\nSOUR
 CE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA co
 mpetency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book diff
 ers or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOME
 S (WEEK 02)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or d
 emonstrate:\n• Analyze series and parallel resistor networks.\n• Use K
 irchhoff's Voltage Law and Kirchhoff's Current Law to reason about circuit
  behavior.\n• Design and analyze a voltage divider\, including the effec
 t of loading.\n• Predict node voltages\, branch currents\, equivalent re
 sistance\, and power.\n• Calculate equivalent resistance\, node/branch v
 alues\, divider outputs\, and power.\n• Use KVL/KCL to check whether cal
 culated results are internally consistent.\n• Use a DMM to verify a DC n
 etwork and explain differences between predicted and measured values.\n•
  Troubleshoot opens\, shorts\, wrong resistor values\, and wiring mistakes
  systematically.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above
  are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still canno
 t explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not cou
 nt that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and u
 se the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\
 nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point for t
 he week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on real har
 dware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMP
 LE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning out
 comes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that 
 one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next availab
 le review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
