 /alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Foundational circuit
  measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → C
 areer Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive
  for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 3 FOCUS: Test Equipment First: DMM + B
 ench Supply + Oscilloscope\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 8.1–8.16\; 11.8–11.8.1\nCA
 REER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Use instruments before later labs require them\; lo
 ading\, probes\, triggering\, current limits\, signal-generator awareness.
 \n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Oscilloscope Basics: https://www.youtube.com
 /watch?v=067W7h1BhxE\n- Function Generator Tutorial: https://www.youtube.c
 om/watch?v=mLKPwWGBtIw\n- ETA CETa competencies: https://www.etai.org/comp
 s/CETa_comps.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Choose the correct instrument and connec
 tion for a stated measurement\; safely power a low-voltage circuit\; captu
 re voltage/time/frequency on a scope and explain loading risk.\n\nSYSTEM R
 ULES: Watching alone nevercounts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code 
 -> build/measure ->debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with
  ~10 minutes ofspaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification 
