 OK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrat
 aSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.
 2 p.13 Tools & Test Equipment + Ch.19 pp.165–175.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.19 
 quiz p.175 after the Saturday instrument lab.\nWHY: You learn instrument c
 hoice\, loading\, meter use and oscilloscope concepts before later labs de
 pend on those tools.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CET
 a textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control wh
 enever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY —
  REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 03)\nBy the end of this event\, you shou
 ld be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Select the correct DMM mode for
  voltage\, resistance\, continuity\, current\, and diode checks.\n• Expl
 ain correct meter placement and why current measurements are different fro
 m voltage measurements.\n• Set a bench supply voltage and current limit 
 and distinguish constant-voltage from constant-current operation.\n• Exp
 lain oscilloscope volts/div\, time/div\, triggering\, coupling\, probe att
 enuation\, and bandwidth at a basic working level.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe 
 assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in thi
 s outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these it
 ems after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the conc
 ept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental r
 esource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assi
 gned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain 
 or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up lis
 t and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet log
 ging is required.
