 c.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 03)\nBy the end of 
 this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Set a benc
 h supply voltage and current limit and distinguish constant-voltage from c
 onstant-current operation.\n• Explain oscilloscope volts/div\, time/div\
 , triggering\, coupling\, probe attenuation\, and bandwidth at a basic wor
 king level.\n• Use proper oscilloscope grounding and understand the haza
 rd of earth-referenced probe grounds.\n• Measure a real low-voltage sign
 al with a DMM\, bench supply\, and oscilloscope and interpret the result.\
