 .youtube.com/playlist?list=PL0o_zxa4K1BV9E-N8tSExU1djL6slnjbL\n\nMASTERY G
 ATE: Convert frequency/period\, identify peak/peak-to-peak/RMS\, explain p
 hase qualitatively\, calculate RCtiming\, and capture an RC waveform.\n\nS
 YSTEM RULES: Watching alonenever counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculat
 e/code -> build/measure-> debug -> document. Start each non-exam study blo
 ck with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justif
 ication for anunhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n
 1. Open LAB-004 — RC Time Constant + Filter Response in Practice → Lab
  Center → Week 04.\n2. Choose one route. Virtual needs: Web browser only
 . Physical needs: Oscilloscope\, function generator\, breadboard\, R/C com
 ponents.\n3. Follow every numbered step under the route you selected\; pre
 dict the result before simulating\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the 
 required evidence: Calculations + two simulator scope captures + short int
 erpretation.\n5. Mark only the route you actually completed. A virtual com
 pletion does not claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEE
 P THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your
  scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT
 .\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\
 nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.3 pp.19–24 
 + Ch.6 pp.45–46.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Fresh problems from the assigned pages\
 ; no answer-key checking until you have committed answers.\nWHY: Builds AC
  waveform\, RMS\, frequency/period\, capacitance\, inductance and first-or
 der reactive behavior.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary C
 ETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control 
 whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY 
 — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 04)\nBy the end of this event\, you s
 hould be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Describe sine waves and basi
 c AC quantities: amplitude\, peak\, peak-to-peak\, frequency\, period\, ph
 ase\, and RMS.\n• Convert between frequency and period and interpret wav
 eform measurements.\n• Explain how capacitors and inductors store energy
  and oppose changes in voltage or current.\n• Describe RC and RL transie
 nt behavior and the idea of a time constant.\n• Calculate frequency/peri
 od\, RMS or peak relationships where assigned\, and basic RC timing quanti
 ties.\n• Read waveform scales accurately and connect numerical results t
 o scope displays.\n• Recognize basic low-pass and high-pass behavior.\n
 • Use an oscilloscope to connect waveform theory to measured circuit beh
 avior.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are inten
 ded to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain 
 or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that it
 em as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the lin
 ked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END 
 MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point for the week. T
 he week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on real hardware/code
 /measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLET
 ION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes belo
 w. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concep
 t on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review 
 block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
