SUMMARY:W06 • Learn — Reactance\, Impedance\, Resonance & Transformers
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=6\n• Search this topic: https://numbercla
 w2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Reactance%20%2B%20Impedance%2
 0%2B%20Resonance%20%2B%20Filters%20%2B%20Transformers\n• Engineering Lib
 rary: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCARE
 ER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital troubleshooting and instrume
 ntation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Comp
 lete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\
 nWEEK 6 FOCUS: Reactance + Impedance + Resonance + Filters + Transformers\
 nETA/CETa SCOPE: 2.1–2.5.1\; 2.10–2.11\; 3.4–3.4.2\; 4.7–4.16\; 9.
 6\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Understand filters\, clocks/crystals\, inducti
 ve loads\, transformer behavior\, resonance and bandwidth/Q without over-s
 pecializing.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n-Capacitors and Inductors playlist
 : https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLB9A78ED3D7EF1AE5\n- oscillators 
 and Multivibrators playlist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLwjK_i
 yK4LLCVdgBR30pSFVj-17TI_8ou\n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.etai.org/C
 ommon_Formulas.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: calculate reactance/resonance\, classi
 fy an RLC network\, explain transformer step-up/down and crystal/oscillato
 r purpose\, and interpret a simple filter response.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watch
 ing alone never counts. Use learn-> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/me
 asure -> debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minut
 es of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an un
 healthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to this
  week’s competencies. Create a one-page summary and 5–10 recall prompt
 s. first 10 min: spaced retrieval from older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB 
 — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: u
 se your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASS
 IGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet
 .pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.5 pp.3
 6–44 + Ch.6 pp.45–52.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.5 quiz p.44 and Ch.6 quiz p.5
 2.\nWHY: This is the book's main reactance/impedance/resonance/filter/tran
 sformer block.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa text
 book. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever
  the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUI
 RED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 06)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be 
 able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain capacitive reactance\, induct
 ive reactance\, impedance\, and their dependence on frequency.\n• Recogn
 ize the relationship among resistance\, reactance\, impedance\, voltage\, 
 current\, and phase.\n• Explain resonance and the role of inductance and
  capacitance in tuned behavior.\n• Describe basic low-pass\, high-pass\,
  band-pass\, and band-stop filter behavior.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigne
 d resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outco
 me list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items aft
 er the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on 
 a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource
  before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned wo
 rk\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demo
 nstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and r
 epair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is
  required.
