 WEEK 06)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demo
 nstrate:\n• Explain capacitive reactance\, inductive reactance\, impedan
 ce\, and their dependence on frequency.\n• Recognize the relationship am
 ong resistance\, reactance\, impedance\, voltage\, current\, and phase.\n
 • Explain resonance and the role of inductance and capacitance in tuned 
 behavior.\n• Describe basic low-pass\, high-pass\, band-pass\, and band-
 stop filter behavior.\n• Calculate basic XL\, XC\, impedance/ratio/reson
 ance relationships at the assigned CETa depth.\n• Predict how changing f
 requency changes circuit behavior.\n• Explain transformer turns ratio\, 
 voltage/current relationships\, isolation\, and basic loading ideas.\n• 
 Use calculations\, simulation\, or measurements to verify frequency-depend
 ent circuit behavior.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks 
 above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still 
 cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do no
 t count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list 
 and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the ga
 p.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point 
