DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=9\n• Search this topic: https://numbercla
 w2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electronic%20Power%20Supplies
 \n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university
 /resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital trouble
 shooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Cor
 e → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repa
 ir or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 9 FOCUS: Power Supplies + Rectifiers + Regulati
 on + Protection\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 10.1–10.11\; 1.4\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPO
 SE: Power trees\, linear vs switching supply\, rectification/filtering/reg
 ulation\, fuse/protection placement\, 3.3V/5 V rail awareness.\n\nTHIS WEE
 K'S RESOURCES:\n- Linear Power Supply: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UTe
 tQhGyUVg\n- Switch-Mode Power Supply: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3FyX
 qNcqvRM\n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n
 \nMASTERY GATE: Trace asupply block diagram\, calculate expected DC output
 s\, identify rectifier/filter/regulator stages\, and isolate one likely su
 pplyfault.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->retri
 eve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start each no
 n-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed s
 ession as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStud
 y only the resources tied to this week’s competencies. Create a one-page
  summary and 5–10 recall prompts. first 10 min: spaced retrieval from ol
 der material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associa
 te CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the P
 RINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://w
 ww.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK AS
 SIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.11 pp.85–90.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.11 quiz p.90.\n
 WHY: The entire chapter maps cleanly to power-supply architecture\, rectif
 ication\, filtering\, regulation and faults.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition
  book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + curre
 nt ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a current t
 opic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 09)\nBy the end 
 of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Describ
 e the functional blocks of an electronic power supply: transformation/conv
 ersion\, rectification\, filtering\, regulation\, and protection.\n• Exp
 lain half-wave/full-wave/bridge rectification and the purpose of filter ca
 pacitors.\n• Distinguish basic linear regulation from switching regulati
 on.\n• Explain ripple\, load regulation\, line regulation\, efficiency\,
  and current limiting at a practical level.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigne
 d resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outco
 me list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items aft
 er the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on 
 a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource
  before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned wo
 rk\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demo
 nstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and r
 epair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is
  required.
