 aSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.
 16 pp.132–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Hold the full Ch.16 quiz until W14 after 
 computer-basics pages are finished.\nWHY: Covers number systems\, logic fa
 milies\, gates\, Boolean logic and sequential circuits before MCU work.\nS
 OURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA
  competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book d
 iffers or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTC
 OMES (WEEK 11)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain o
 r demonstrate:\n• Convert among binary\, decimal\, and hexadecimal and u
 se binary place value confidently.\n• Explain Boolean logic and the beha
 vior/truth tables of NOT\, AND\, OR\, NAND\, NOR\, XOR\, and XNOR.\n• Di
 stinguish combinational from sequential logic and recognize latches/flip-f
 lops/counters at a basic level.\n• Explain logic-high/logic-low levels\,
  noise margins\, pull-ups/pull-downs\, floating inputs\, and open-drain/op
 en-collector concepts.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks
  above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still
  cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do n
 ot count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list
  and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the g
 ap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the l
 earning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, 
 write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the n
 ext available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
