 gic + Number Systems + Boolean + Logic Families\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 13.1–13
 .12\; 9.4–9.5\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Binary/hex\, truth tables\, TTL/
 CMOS levels\, flip-flops\, counters\, clocks\, buses\, pull-ups/pull-downs
  and floating inputs.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Digital Electronics —
  ALL ABOUT ELECTRONICS: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLwjK_iyK4LL
 BC_so3odA64E2MLgIRKafl\n- Digital Electronics — Neso Academy: https://ww
 w.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLBlnK6fEyqRjMH3mWf6kwqiTbT798eAOm\n\nMASTERY 
 GATE: Convert number systems\, build truth tables\, explain TTL/CMOS level
 s and sequential devices\, and diagnose a floating-input/logic-state fault
 .\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone nevercounts. Use learn -> retrieve -> ca
 lculate/code -> build/measure ->debug -> document. Start each non-exam stu
 dy block with ~10 minutes ofspaced recall. Never use a missed session as j
