 6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.16 pp.132–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Hold th
 e full Ch.16 quiz until W14 after computer-basics pages are finished.\nWHY
 : Covers number systems\, logic families\, gates\, Boolean logic and seque
 ntial circuits before MCU work.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the 
 primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata
  control whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTE
 R TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 11)\nBy the end of this event
 \, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Distinguish combinat
 ional from sequential logic and recognize latches/flip-flops/counters at a
  basic level.\n• Explain logic-high/logic-low levels\, noise margins\, p
 ull-ups/pull-downs\, floating inputs\, and open-drain/open-collector conce
 pts.\n• Recognize memory\, buses\, ports\, and basic digital-system bloc
 ks.\n• Verify digital behavior using truth tables\, simulation\, or meas
 ured logic signals.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks ab
 ove are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still ca
 nnot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not 
 count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list an
 d use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.
 \n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the lear
 ning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, wri
 te that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next
  available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
