DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=13\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Schematics%20%2B%20Troublesh
 ooting\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-univ
 ersity/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital t
 roubleshooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Care
 er Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive fo
 r repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 13 FOCUS: Schematics + Block/Wiring Diagr
 ams + Systematic Troubleshooting\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 6.1–6.10\; 8.× reinfo
 rcement\; 21.4/21.7 preview\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: signal tracing\, tes
 t points\, pinouts\, datasheets\, expected-vs-actual measurements\, reprod
 uce→measure→isolate→verify.\n\nTHIS week's resources:\n- PRIMARY —
  SparkFun How to Read a Schematic: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/ho
 w-to-read-a-schematic/overview\n\nMASTERY GATE: Trace power/signal flow on
  an unfamiliar diagram\, choose next test points\, locate a seeded fault\,
  and write a concise defect/root-cause note.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alo
 ne never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -
 > debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of s
 paced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy
  make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to this week
 ’s competencies. Create a one-page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. fi
 rst 10 min: spaced retrieval from older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEE
 P THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your
  scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT
 .\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\
 nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.18 pp.159–1
 64 + selected Ch.19 pp.165–175 review + Appendix C pp.217–218.\nQUIZ /
  REVIEW: Ch.18 quiz p.164 + Unit 8 review p.181.\nWHY: This is the book's 
 strongest troubleshooting/diagram/test-point block and directly supports e
 ngineering-lab work.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CET
 a textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control wh
 enever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY —
  REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 13)\nBy the end of this event\, you shou
 ld be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Read basic schematics\, block d
 iagrams\, wiring diagrams\, pinouts\, connector tables\, and signal-flow d
 rawings.\n• Trace power and signals from source to destination and relat
 e schematic symbols to physical hardware.\n• Use datasheets to find pin 
 functions\, ratings\, timing\, operating conditions\, and reference circui
 ts.\n• Apply a systematic troubleshooting loop: verify symptom\, gather 
 evidence\, divide/isolate\, form hypothesis\, test\, repair\, verify.\n\nC
 OVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cove
 r every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstr
 ate one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as compl
 ete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked officia
 l or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RU
 LE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If 
 you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a
  short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block.
  No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
