 versity/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/digital 
 troubleshooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Car
 eer Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive f
 or repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 13 FOCUS: Schematics + Block/Wiring Diag
 rams + Systematic Troubleshooting\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 6.1–6.10\; 8.× reinf
 orcement\; 21.4/21.7 preview\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: signal tracing\, te
 st points\, pinouts\, datasheets\, expected-vs-actual measurements\, repro
 duce→measure→isolate→verify.\n\nTHIS week's resources:\n- PRIMARY 
 — SparkFun How to Read a Schematic: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials
 /how-to-read-a-schematic/overview\n\nMASTERY GATE: Trace power/signal flow
  on an unfamiliar diagram\, choose next test points\, locate a seeded faul
 t\, and write a concise defect/root-cause note.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching 
 alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measur
 e -> debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes o
 f spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unheal
 thy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-013 — 
 Schematic Signal Tracing + Root Cause in Practice → Lab Center → Week 
 13.\n2. Choose one route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physical needs:
  Known circuit/simulation\, schematic\, DMM/scope.\n3. Follow every number
 ed step under the route you selected\; predict the result before simulatin
 g\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the required evidence: Annotated sch
 ematic + measurement trail + fault tree + root-cause report.\n5. Mark only
  the route you actually completed. A virtual completion does not claim phy
 sical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Offici
 al Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy
  and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata:
  https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — 
 V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.18 pp.159–164 + selected Ch.19 pp.165
 –175 review + Appendix C pp.217–218.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.18 quiz p.164 
 + Unit 8 review p.181.\nWHY: This is the book's strongest troubleshooting/
 diagram/test-point block and directly supports engineering-lab work.\nSOUR
 CE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA co
 mpetency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book diff
 ers or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOME
 S (WEEK 13)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or d
 emonstrate:\n• Read basic schematics\, block diagrams\, wiring diagrams\
 , pinouts\, connector tables\, and signal-flow drawings.\n• Trace power 
 and signals from source to destination and relate schematic symbols to phy
 sical hardware.\n• Use datasheets to find pin functions\, ratings\, timi
 ng\, operating conditions\, and reference circuits.\n• Apply a systemati
 c troubleshooting loop: verify symptom\, gather evidence\, divide/isolate\
 , form hypothesis\, test\, repair\, verify.\n• Use diagram/signal-path i
 nformation to choose measurement points and isolate a fault.\n• Interpre
 t expected values from a schematic before probing.\n• Use signal tracing
 \, substitution/known-good comparison\, continuity\, voltage\, and wavefor
 m checks appropriately.\n• Distinguish root cause from symptom and docum
 ent a defensible troubleshooting conclusion.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assign
 ed resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outc
 ome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items af
 ter the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on
  a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resourc
 e before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the 
 cumulative proof point for the week. The week is Green only when the knowl
 edge can be used on real hardware/code/measurements without following a st
 ep-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\,
  then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstr
 ate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repai
 r it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is req
 uired.
