SUMMARY:W14 • Learn — C Fundamentals + Computer Architecture
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=14\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=C%20Programming%20I%20%2B%20
 Computer%20Architecture\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-u
 p + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core 
 → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep
  Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 14 FOCUS: C Programming I + Compu
 ter Architecture\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 15.1–15.4\; 15.6–15.9\; 3.8\nCAREER/
 EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Compiler/linker\, types\, control flow\, functions\, arr
 ays\, structs\, memory blocks\, CPU/buses/peripherals.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESO
 URCES:\n- Beej’s Guide to C: https://beej.us/guide/bgc/\n- Crash Course 
 Computer Science: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL8dPuuaLjXtNlUrzy
 H5r6jN9ulIgZBpdo\n\nMASTERY GATE: Write and explain a small C program from
  scratch\; explain CPU/RAM/flash/peripherals/bus blocks and how software r
 eaches hardware.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -
 >retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start e
 ach non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a mi
 ssed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:
 \nStudy only the resources tied to this week’s competencies. Create a on
 e-page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. first 10 min: spaced retrieval f
 rom older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official A
 ssociate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and
  the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: htt
 ps://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 B
 OOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Finish Ch.16 pp.144–147 + Ch.17 pp.149–153
 .\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.16 quiz p.148.\nWHY: Book provides computer/microproc
 essor architecture while external C resources teach actual programming dep
 th.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Curre
 nt ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older 
 book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNIN
 G OUTCOMES (WEEK 14)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to exp
 lain or demonstrate:\n• Explain the build path from C source through com
 piler/linker to an executable/firmware image.\n• Use integer types\, fix
 ed-width types\, variables\, operators\, conditionals\, loops\, functions\
 , arrays\, strings\, structs\, and enums.\n• Explain scope\, lifetime\, 
 and basic memory organization.\n• Describe CPU\, RAM\, flash\, buses\, p
 eripherals\, registers\, inputs\, and outputs in a microcontroller/compute
 r system.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are in
 tended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot expla
 in or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that
  item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the 
 linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE
  COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outco
 mes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that on
 e concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available
  review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
