 fred-university/week.html?week=14\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=C%20Programming%20I%20%2B%20
 Computer%20Architecture\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-u
 p + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core 
 → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep
  Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 14 FOCUS: C Programming I + Compu
 ter Architecture\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 15.1–15.4\; 15.6–15.9\; 3.8\nCAREER/
 EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Compiler/linker\, types\, control flow\, functions\, arr
 ays\, structs\, memory blocks\, CPU/buses/peripherals.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESO
 URCES:\n- Beej’s Guide to C: https://beej.us/guide/bgc/\n- Crash Course 
 Computer Science: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL8dPuuaLjXtNlUrzy
 H5r6jN9ulIgZBpdo\n\nMASTERY GATE: Write and explain a small C program from
  scratch\; explain CPU/RAM/flash/peripherals/bus blocks and how software r
 eaches hardware.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -
 >retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start e
 ach non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a mi
 ssed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:
 \nWork fresh calculations/recognition questions without notes. Use the off
 icial formula sheet when allowed. Target≥80%\; every miss gets an ETA co
 mpetency number and written correction.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LI
 NKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/G
 oogle Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA
  6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL 
 STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Finish Ch.16 pp.144–147 
 + Ch.17 pp.149–153.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.16 quiz p.148.\nWHY: Book provide
 s computer/microprocessor architecture while external C resources teach ac
 tual programming depth.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary 
 CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control
  whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY 
 — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 14)\nBy the end of this event\, you s
 hould be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain the build path from 
 C source through compiler/linker to an executable/firmware image.\n• Use
  integer types\, fixed-width types\, variables\, operators\, conditionals\
 , loops\, functions\, arrays\, strings\, structs\, and enums.\n• Explain
  scope\, lifetime\, and basic memory organization.\n• Describe CPU\, RAM
 \, flash\, buses\, peripherals\, registers\, inputs\, and outputs in a mic
 rocontroller/computer system.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources an
 d tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If yo
 u still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session
 \, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-
 up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closin
 g the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then chec
 k the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an out
 come\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it durin
 g the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
