 rtual route: web browser plus the linked Wokwi STM32 simulator.\n3. Physic
 al route: supported STM32 Nucleo/development board\; USB data cable (not c
 harge-only)\; computer\; STM32Cube IDE/CubeMX\; on-board ST-LINK or compat
 ible SWD debugger\; breadboard\; jumper wires\; LED and current-limiting r
 esistor if the board's built-in LED is not used\; DMM\; oscilloscope optio
 nal.\n4. Confirm the board is recognized by the computer\, the correct boa
 rd/debugger target is selected\, and all external signals use compatible l
 ogic voltage.\n5. If hardware or drivers are not ready\, use Wokwi so the 
 scheduled work continues.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Offi
 cial Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive co
 py and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errat
 a: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRE
