SUMMARY:W15 • Lab — Build & Debug an Embedded C State Machine
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=15\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=C%20Programming%20II%20%2B%2
 0Embedded%20C%20%2B%20State%20Machines\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw
 2.github.io/alfred-university/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://
 numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION:
  C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORI
 TY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work fi
 rst\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 15 FOCUS: C Program
 ming II + Embedded C + State Machines\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 15.5–15.7\; 13.12
  reinforcement\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Pointers\, arrays/strings\, struc
 ts/enums\, .c/.h modules\, bitwise masks\, const/volatile\, FSMs\, blockin
 g vs nonblocking design.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Beej’s Guide to C:
  https://beej.us/guide/bgc/\n- STM32 MCU Developer Zone: https://www.st.co
 m/content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Write m
 odular C using pointers/structs/enums/bit operations and explain a finite-
 state-machine design without copying atutorial.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching 
 alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measur
 e -> debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes o
 f spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unheal
 thy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-015 — 
 Embedded C State Machine in Practice → Lab Center → Week 15.\n2. Choos
 e one route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physical needs: C environmen
 t or MCU board.\n3. Follow every numbered step under the route you selecte
 d\; predict the result before simulating\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Sa
 ve the required evidence: State diagram + source code + transition log + o
 ne error-case explanation.\n5. Mark only the route you actually completed.
  A virtual completion does not claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFEREN
 CE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th
  ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in B
 OOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErra
 taSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch
 .17 pp.153–156.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.17 quiz p.156 + Unit 7 review pp.157
 –158.\nWHY: Book supplies programming/control concepts\; Beej/C exercise
 s provide the real code-writing skill needed for the transition.\nSOURCE R
 ULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA compet
 ency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs 
 or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (W
 EEK 15)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demon
 strate:\n• Use pointers\, addresses\, dereferencing\, arrays/pointers\, 
 structs\, and function interfaces safely at a practical level.\n• Use bi
 twise AND/OR/XOR\, shifts\, masks\, and set/clear/test operations for hard
 ware-oriented code.\n• Explain const\, volatile\, macros\, headers/modul
 es\, and compiler warnings in embedded C.\n• Distinguish blocking from n
 onblocking behavior.\n• Work bit-mask/shift examples and pointer/address
  reasoning without guessing.\n• Trace state-machine transitions and timi
 ng/interrupt-related behavior.\n• Design and implement a finite-state ma
 chine for simple embedded behavior.\n• Explain the role of interrupts/ti
 mers conceptually and write modular code that is easier to test/debug.\n\n
 COVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cov
 er every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonst
 rate one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as comp
 lete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked offici
 al or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RU
 LE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point for the week. The week is
  Green only when the knowledge can be used on real hardware/code/measureme
 nts without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\n
 Finish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you 
 cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a sho
 rt catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block. No 
 spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
