SUMMARY:W17 • Prep — UART & Python Tools
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=17\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=UART%20%2B%20Python%20Serial
 \n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university
 /resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + debu
 g instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep 
 Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra
  depth.\n\nNeed by Week 17. Confirm working USB/serial path (board virtual
  COM is acceptable)\, cable/driver\, terminal program\, Python environment
 \, pySerial\, and a test COM/tty workflow.\n\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST
 :\n1. Open LAB-017 in Practice → Lab Center → Week 17.\n2. Virtual rou
 te: web browser plus Wokwi and a browser-based Python environment from the
  lab links.\n3. Physical route: STM32/development board\; USB data cable\;
  working virtual COM port or USB-to-UART adapter with shared ground\; corr
 ect driver\; terminal program\; Python 3\; pySerial\; logic analyzer optio
 nal.\n4. Confirm the serial port appears\, TX/RX voltage levels are compat
 ible\, TX connects to RX\, grounds are common\, and the selected baud/form
 at settings match.\n5. Run a simple transmit/receive test before the sched
 uled integration lab.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official
  Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy a
 nd the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: h
 ttps://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LE
 ARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain 
 or demonstrate:\n• Know what equipment/parts are required for the next p
 ractical session and what each item is for.\n• Confirm every critical it
 em is ready\, compatible\, and safe to use before the lab begins.\n• Ide
 ntify any missing item early enough to obtain or substitute it without can
 celling the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and t
 asks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you s
 till cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, 
 do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up 
 list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing t
 he gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check t
 he learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcom
 e\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during t
 he next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Equipment\,Embedded\,CETa
