SUMMARY:W16 • Learn — STM32 Setup\, GPIO & SWD
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=16\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=STM32%20Setup%20%2B%20GPIO%2
 0%2B%20SWD%20Debug\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io
 /alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + s
 erial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Car
 eer Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive f
 or repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 16 FOCUS: HOLIDAY LIGHT: STM32 Setup + G
 PIO + SWD Debug\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 13.12\; 15.3/15.6\; 12.1–12.3 reinforce
 ment\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: CubeIDE\, build/flash\, Cortex-M basics\, G
 PIO\, pin mux\, breakpoints\, watch variables/registers\; no Christmas Eve
  session.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32Cube IDE: https://www.st.com/c
 ontent/st_com/en/stm32cubeide.html\n- STM32 MCU Developer Zone: https://ww
 w.st.com/content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: 
 Build/flash a GPIO project\, use breakpoints/watch\, explain the major bui
 ld/debug steps\, and document one real debug issue.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watch
 ing alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/m
 easure -> debug ->document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minut
 es of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an un
 healthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nInstall/verify CubeIDE\, create proje
 ct\, map MCU/flash/RAM/GPIO/SWD concepts. First 10 min: cumulative CETarec
 all.\n\nOFFICIAL STM32 REFERENCES:\n• STM32Cube IDE: https://www.st.com/
 content/st_com/en/stm32cubeide.html\n• STM32Cube IDE Basics MOOC: https:
 //www.st.com/content/st_com/en/support/learning/stm32-moocs/STM32CubeIDE_b
 asics_MOOC.html\n• STM32Cube MX & CubeHAL Basics MOOC: https://www.st.co
 m/content/st_com/en/support/learning/stm32-moocs/stm32cubemx-and-cubeHhal-
 basics.html\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate
  CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRI
 NTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www
 .etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSI
 GNMENT\nREAD / USE: Targeted Ch.17 pp.149–155 review while setting up ST
 M32.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Explain MPU/memory/I/O/control blocks without notes b
 efore the GPIO lab.\nWHY: The book gives architecture vocabulary\; STM32 p
 ractice turns it into real MCU bring-up/debug capability.\nSOURCE RULE: Th
 e 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wo
 rding + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omit
 s a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 16)
 \nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:
 \n• Explain what an MCU and ARM Cortex-M core are and identify flash\, R
 AM\, GPIO\, clocks\, and peripherals in an STM32 system.\n• Create/confi
 gure a basic STM32 project in STM32Cube IDE/CubeMX.\n• Configure GPIO in
 put/output and understand pin multiplexing at a working level.\n• Build\
 , flash\, run\, and reset firmware on a real board.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe
  assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in th
 is outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these i
 tems after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the con
 cept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental 
 resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the ass
 igned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain
  or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up li
 st and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet lo
 gging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
