SUMMARY:W16 • Build — Flash STM32 Firmware & Debug with SWD
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=16\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=STM32%20Setup%20%2B%20GPIO%2
 0%2B%20SWD%20Debug\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io
 /alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + s
 erial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Car
 eer Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive f
 or repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 16 FOCUS: HOLIDAY LIGHT: STM32 Setup + G
 PIO + SWD Debug\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 13.12\; 15.3/15.6\; 12.1–12.3 reinforce
 ment\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: CubeIDE\, build/flash\, Cortex-M basics\, G
 PIO\, pin mux\, breakpoints\, watch variables/registers\; no Christmas Eve
  session.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32Cube IDE: https://www.st.com/c
 ontent/st_com/en/stm32cubeide.html\n- STM32 MCU Developer Zone: https://ww
 w.st.com/content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: 
 Build/flash a GPIO project\, use breakpoints/watch\, explain the major bui
 ld/debug steps\, and document one real debug issue.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watch
 ing alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/m
 easure -> debug ->document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minut
 es of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an un
 healthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nBuild and flash a simple GPIO project
 . Practice breakpoint\, step\, watch variable/register. Record one issue a
 nd fix.\n\nOFFICIAL STM32 REFERENCES:\n• STM32Cube IDE: https://www.st.c
 om/content/st_com/en/stm32cubeide.html\n• STM32Cube IDE Basics MOOC: htt
 ps://www.st.com/content/st_com/en/support/learning/stm32-moocs/STM32CubeID
 E_basics_MOOC.html\n• STM32Cube MX & CubeHAL Basics MOOC: https://www.st
 .com/content/st_com/en/support/learning/stm32-moocs/stm32cubemx-and-cubeHh
 al-basics.html\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associ
 ate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the 
 PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://
 www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK A
 SSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Targeted Ch.17 pp.149–155 review while setting up
  STM32.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Explain MPU/memory/I/O/control blocks without note
 s before the GPIO lab.\nWHY: The book gives architecture vocabulary\; STM3
 2 practice turns it into real MCU bring-up/debug capability.\nSOURCE RULE:
  The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency
  wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or o
 mits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 
 16)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstra
 te:\n• Configure GPIO input/output and understand pin multiplexing at a 
 working level.\n• Build\, flash\, run\, and reset firmware on a real boa
 rd.\n• Use SWD debugging: breakpoints\, single-step\, watch variables\, 
 and basic register inspection.\n• Separate a firmware problem from a boa
 rd/power/configuration problem during bring-up.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe ass
 igned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this o
 utcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items
  after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept
  on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental reso
 urce before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigne
 d work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or 
 demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list a
 nd repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet loggin
 g is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
