SUMMARY:W18 • Prep — Logic Analyzer + I²C/SPI Hardware
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=18\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=I2C/SPI%20%2B%20Logic%20Anal
 yzer%20%2B%20Sensors/Actuators\n• Engineering Library: https://numbercla
 w2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU 
 bring-up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa 
 Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use
  Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nNeed by Week 18. Confirm logic an
 alyzer and leads\, one supported I2C or SPI sensor/peripheral breakout\, j
 umper wires\, pull-ups if required\, datasheet\, and safe voltage compatib
 ility with the MCU.\n\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-018 in P
 ractice → Lab Center → Week 18.\n2. Virtual route: web browser plus th
 e linked Wokwi I²C/SPI simulation.\n3. Physical route: STM32/development 
 board\; one documented I²C or SPI sensor breakout\; USB data cable\; brea
 dboard and jumper wires\; logic analyzer with leads\; device datasheet\; p
 ull-up resistors if the breakout does not include them.\n4. Confirm 3.3 V/
 5 V compatibility\, pinout\, ground\, bus type\, I²C address or SPI chip-
 select wiring\, and analyzer input limits before power.\n5. If the hardwar
 e combination is uncertain or incomplete\, use the virtual route rather th
 an guessing at connections.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Of
 ficial Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive 
 copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. err
 ata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUI
 RED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to ex
 plain or demonstrate:\n• Know what equipment/parts are required for the 
 next practical session and what each item is for.\n• Confirm every criti
 cal item is ready\, compatible\, and safe to use before the lab begins.\n
 • Identify any missing item early enough to obtain or substitute it with
