DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=17\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=UART%20%2B%20Python%20Serial
 \n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university
 /resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + debu
 g instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep 
 Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra
  depth.\n\nWEEK 17 FOCUS: HOLIDAY LIGHT: UART + Python Serial + Computer A
 pplications\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 16.1–16.10\; 12.1–12.4\nCAREER/EMBEDDED P
 URPOSE: UART framing/baud\, terminal use\, Python pySerial logging\, basic
  software/storage/backups/networking\; no New Year’s Eve session.\n\nTHI
 S WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Serial Communication — SparkFun: https://learn.sp
 arkfun.com/tutorials/serial-communication/all\n-pySerial docs: https://pys
 erial.readthedocs.io/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Send/receive MCU serial data\, pars
 e/log it in Python\, explain basic computer/software/networking concepts\,
  and recover from a malformed response.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone ne
 ver counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> deb
 ug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced
  recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make
 -up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nLearn TX/RX/GND\, framing/baud\, terminal use. Im
 plement MCU status output.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Off
 icial Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive c
 opy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. erra
 ta: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE 
 — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.16 pp.144–146 ports/interfaces + 
 selected Ch.17 pp.149–155.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Short current-competency reca
 ll set\; book is background\, not the whole UART/Python skill.\nWHY: The 2
 016 book covers computer/port concepts but external UART and Python materi
 al is required for current practical depth.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition 
 book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + curren
 t ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a current to
 pic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 17)\nBy the end o
 f this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain 
 UART TX\, RX\, ground/reference\, baud rate\, frame format\, and asynchron
 ous serial communication.\n• Send and receive UART data between an STM32
  and a host computer.\n• Use a terminal/serial monitor to inspect traffi
 c and diagnose basic framing/configuration problems.\n• Use Python/pySer
 ial to open a port\, configure timeout/baud\, send commands\, read respons
 es\, and close cleanly.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and task
 s above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you stil
 l cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do 
 not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up lis
 t and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the 
 gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the 
 learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\,
  write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the 
 next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
