 l\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-universit
 y/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + deb
 ug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep
  Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extr
 a depth.\n\nWEEK 17 FOCUS: HOLIDAY LIGHT: UART + Python Serial + Computer 
 Applications\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 16.1–16.10\; 12.1–12.4\nCAREER/EMBEDDED 
 PURPOSE: UART framing/baud\, terminal use\, Python pySerial logging\, basi
 c software/storage/backups/networking\; no New Year’s Eve session.\n\nTH
 IS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Serial Communication — SparkFun: https://learn.s
 parkfun.com/tutorials/serial-communication/all\n-pySerial docs: https://py
 serial.readthedocs.io/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Send/receive MCU serial data\, par
 se/log it in Python\, explain basic computer/software/networking concepts\
 , and recover from a malformed response.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone n
 ever counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> de
 bug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of space
 d recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy mak
 e-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-017 — UART + 
 Python Serial Console in Practice → Lab Center → Week 17.\n2. Choose o
 ne route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physical needs: STM32 board\, U
 SB/UART path\, Python + pySerial\, logic analyzer optional.\n3. Follow eve
 ry numbered step under the route you selected\; predict the result before 
 simulating\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the required evidence: Firm
 ware + Python host script + serial-terminal capture + protocol/error note.
 \n5. Mark only the route you actually completed. A virtual completion does
  not claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINK
 S:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Goo
 gle Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6
 th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL ST
 UDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.16 pp.144–146 ports/int
 erfaces + selected Ch.17 pp.149–155.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Short current-compe
 tency recall set\; book is background\, not the whole UART/Python skill.\n
 WHY: The 2016 book covers computer/port concepts but external UART and Pyt
 hon material is required for current practical depth.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6t
 h-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wordin
 g + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a 
 current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 17)\nBy
  the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n
 • Explain UART TX\, RX\, ground/reference\, baud rate\, frame format\, a
 nd asynchronous serial communication.\n• Send and receive UART data betw
 een an STM32 and a host computer.\n• Use a terminal/serial monitor to in
 spect traffic and diagnose basic framing/configuration problems.\n• Use 
 Python/pySerial to open a port\, configure timeout/baud\, send commands\, 
 read responses\, and close cleanly.\n• Parse and log basic device respon
 ses from Python.\n• Explain how a host-side application can test or cont
 rol an embedded device.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and task
 s above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you stil
 l cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do 
 not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up lis
 t and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the 
 gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof poin
 t for the week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on r
 eal hardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.\
 n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learn
 ing outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, writ
 e that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next 
 available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
