 rent ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the olde
 r book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARN
 ING OUTCOMES (WEEK 18)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to e
 xplain or demonstrate:\n• Explain I2C controller/target roles\, SDA/SCL\
 , addressing\, pull-ups\, start/stop\, read/write\, ACK/NACK\, and basic t
 ransactions.\n• Explain SPI controller/peripheral roles\, SCLK\, MOSI\, 
 MISO\, chip select\, transaction framing\, and the idea of clock mode.\n
 • Choose I2C or SPI appropriately for a simple peripheral and wire it co
 rrectly.\n• Use a logic analyzer to capture and decode UART and the chos
 en I2C/SPI bus.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above 
 are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot
  explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not coun
 t that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and us
