 ault\, and drive/read a real peripheral.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone n
 ever counts. Use learn -> retrieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> de
 bug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of space
 d recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy mak
 e-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nApply the concept in LTspice\, C\, STM32\, schem
 atic analysis or bench planning as appropriate. Predict results before sim
 ulation/code execution\; deliberately create one fault when safe.\n\nREFER
 ENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6
 th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in
  BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTEr
 rataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: 
 Use Ch.16/17 as reference only\; current ETA competency wording + I2C/SPI 
 tutorials control the interface lesson.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Unit 7 review pp.1
 57–158 as cumulative digital review.\nWHY: I2C/SPI/modern interface expe
 ctations are not fully covered by this older book\, so current ETA + hands
 -on resources fill the gap.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the prim
 ary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata con
 trol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TO
 DAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 18)\nBy the end of this event\, y
 ou should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Choose I2C or SPI approp
 riately for a simple peripheral and wire it correctly.\n• Use a logic an
 alyzer to capture and decode UART and the chosen I2C/SPI bus.\n• Integra
 te a real sensor/peripheral and convert raw data into meaningful units.\n
 • Interface a digital input/output or actuator safely and verify the end
 -to-end signal path.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks a
 bove are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still c
 annot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not
  count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list a
 nd use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap
 .\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the lea
 rning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, wr
 ite that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the nex
 t available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
