 2.github.io/alfred-university/assessments.html\n• Engineering Library: h
 ttps://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONN
 ECTION: C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE
  PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required 
 work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 18 FOCUS: I2
 C/SPI + Logic Analyzer + Sensors/Actuators\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5\; 13.5/13
 .7–13.12\; 8.10–8.12 reinforcement\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: One real 
 I2C or SPI peripheral\, bus capture\, pull-ups/chip-select/clocking\, sens
 or units\, PWM/output control.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial 
 — SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial
  — SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-peripheral-inte
 rface-spi/all\n- Saleae support: https://support.saleae.com/\n\nMASTERY GA
 TE: Implement one board-level bus\, capture and interpret transactions\, d
 iagnose one bus fault\, and drive/read a real peripheral.\n\nSYSTEM RULES:
  Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve ->calculate/code -> bu
 ild/measure -> debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10
  minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for
  an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LA
 B-018 — I²C / SPI Sensor + Logic Analyzer in Practice → Lab Center 
 → Week 18.\n2. Choose one route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physic
 al needs: STM32 board\, I²C/SPI sensor\, logic analyzer\, datasheet.\n3. 
 Follow every numbered step under the route you selected\; predict the resu
 lt before simulating\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the required evid
 ence: Virtual wiring diagram + code + decoded analyzer capture + data tabl
 e + error case.\n5. Mark only the route you actually completed. A virtual 
 completion does not claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — 
 KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use y
 our scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNM
 ENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf
 \n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Use Ch.16/17 
 as reference only\; current ETA competency wording + I2C/SPI tutorials con
 trol the interface lesson.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Unit 7 review pp.157–158 as c
 umulative digital review.\nWHY: I2C/SPI/modern interface expectations are 
 not fully covered by this older book\, so current ETA + hands-on resources
  fill the gap.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa text
 book. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever
  the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUI
 RED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 18)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be 
 able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain I2C controller/target roles\,
  SDA/SCL\, addressing\, pull-ups\, start/stop\, read/write\, ACK/NACK\, an
 d basic transactions.\n• Explain SPI controller/peripheral roles\, SCLK\
 , MOSI\, MISO\, chip select\, transaction framing\, and the idea of clock 
 mode.\n• Choose I2C or SPI appropriately for a simple peripheral and wir
 e it correctly.\n• Use a logic analyzer to capture and decode UART and t
 he chosen I2C/SPI bus.\n• Integrate a real sensor/peripheral and convert
  raw data into meaningful units.\n• Interface a digital input/output or 
 actuator safely and verify the end-to-end signal path.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\n
 The assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in
  this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of thes
 e items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the 
 concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplement
 al resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practic
 al is the cumulative proof point for the week. The week is Green only when
  the knowledge can be used on real hardware/code/measurements without foll
 owing a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assig
 ned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain o
 r demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list
  and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logg
 ing is required.
