SUMMARY:W19 • Learn — Cabling\, Audio/Video & Optical Systems
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=19\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Cabling%20%2B%20Audio/Video%
 20%2B%20Optical\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Broad CETa general-elec
 tronics coverage plus mixed-domain troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CE
 Ta Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; 
 use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 19 FOCUS: CETa-Specific C
 ompression: Cabling + Audio/Video + Optical\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 7.1–7.13\; 
 17.1–17.9\; 18.1–18.7\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Exam-focused depth for
  low-overlap material\; hands-on cable/connector recognition still support
 s technician roles.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Fiber Optic Lecture Serie
 s: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLC7CC6B17EF009849\n- BNC Connect
 or on RG-58: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ktQVwfo-s9w\n- How Do Speaker
 s Work?: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jhg90zsjqt4\n- How Does an LCD Sc
 reen Work?: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RZacFDPW_34\n\nMASTERY GATE: i
 dentify cable/display/audio/optical devices\, choose termination/test meth
 ods\, explain likely fault symptoms\, and score ≥80% on the section quiz
 .\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> ca
 lculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start each non-exam st
 udy block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as
  justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min:
  spaced recall from prior weeks. Study this week’s scoped material and m
 ake a one-page memory summary. Complete8–12 fresh CETa questions when ET
 A content applies. School work takes priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\n
 REFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guid
 e\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbe
 rs in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEd
 ASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / 
 USE: Ch.14 pp.113–119 + Ch.21 pp.182–187 + Ch.9 optical-semiconductor 
 section pp.76–77.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.14 quiz p.119 + Ch.21 quiz p.187.\n
 WHY: Uses the book for transmission/cabling and technician procedures\; cu
 rrent ETA/video crosswalk fills fiber/audio-video gaps not covered as dedi
 cated chapters.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa tex
 tbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control wheneve
 r the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQU
 IRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 19)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be
  able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Recognize common cable\, connector\,
  transmission-media\, audio/video\, and optical/fiber concepts in the CETa
  scope.\n• Explain basic impedance\, shielding\, grounding\, connector i
 ntegrity\, continuity\, and signal-loss concerns for cabling.\n• Describ
 e basic audio/video signal paths and common failure points at a technician
  level.\n• Explain basic optical/fiber concepts\, source/path/receiver t
 hinking\, attenuation\, and handling cautions.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assi
 gned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this ou
 tcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items 
 after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept 
 on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resou
 rce before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned
  work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or d
 emonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list an
 d repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging
  is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
