  OUTCOMES (WEEK 19)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to expl
 ain or demonstrate:\n• Recognize common cable\, connector\, transmission
 -media\, audio/video\, and optical/fiber concepts in the CETa scope.\n• 
 Explain basic impedance\, shielding\, grounding\, connector integrity\, co
 ntinuity\, and signal-loss concerns for cabling.\n• Describe basic audio
 /video signal paths and common failure points at a technician level.\n• 
 Explain basic optical/fiber concepts\, source/path/receiver thinking\, att
 enuation\, and handling cautions.\n• Select appropriate basic test/troub
 leshooting methods for cables and media.\n• Distinguish this CETa breadt
 h knowledge from the deeper embedded/hardware core.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe
  assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in th
 is outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these i
