 com material while also learning the documentation behavior that matters i
 n real technical jobs.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary C
 ETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control 
 whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY 
 — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 20)\nBy the end of this event\, you s
 hould be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain introductory RF conc
 epts: frequency bands\, propagation\, modulation\, transmission lines\, an
 tennas\, and standing-wave/impedance ideas at CETa level.\n• Recognize b
 asic transmitter/receiver and telecom/telephone signal-path concepts.\n•
  Understand technician procedures involving documentation\, records\, prof
 essionalism\, and technical communication.\n• Relate RF/telecom symptoms
  to likely path\, connector\, configuration\, or signal problems.\n\nCOVER
 AGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover ev
 ery item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate 
 one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as complete.
  Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or
