 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=21\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=CETa%20Final%20Review%20I\n
 • Assessment Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/ass
 essments.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Broad CETa general-electr
 onics coverage plus mixed-domain troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa
  Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; us
 e Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 21 FOCUS: CETa Final Review
  I: Formula + Component + Diagram + Safety Gates\nETA/CETa SCOPE: All 1.0
 –21.0\; official errata applied\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Consolidate wi
 thout pausing embedded momentum\; begin Project 1 requirements/block diagr
 am during non-exam work.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- ETA CETa competencie
 s: https://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n- ETA Common Formulas: https
 ://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n- ETA 6th Ed. Errata: https://www.eta
 i.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n- ETA electronics page: https://www.etai.or
 g/electronics.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Formula drill≥90%\; component/diagra
 m/safety gates green\; Saturday: Book Practice Exam #1 under 2-hour limit\
 ; map every miss to an ETA competency row.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone
  never counts. Use learn-> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> 
 debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spa
 ced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy m
 ake-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min cumulative recall. Work fresh for
 mulas from the official sheet to ≥90%. Identify unfamiliar component sym
 bols/packages/ratings. Apply current ETA errata.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP
  THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your 
 scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.
 \n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\n
 OFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Review formula p.
 224\, symbol/reference p.222\, Appendix C pp.217–218\, weak chapter quiz
 zes and current ETA errata.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Saturday: Book Practice Exam #
 1\, pp.194–201\, under a 2-hour limit. Map every miss to the current ETA
  competency number.\nWHY: The book practice exam checks broad recall\, whi
 le current ETA competency rows prevent outdated book coverage from definin
 g readiness.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbo
 ok. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever t
 he older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRE
 D LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 21)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be ab
 le to explain or demonstrate:\n• Recall and apply the core formula famil
 ies required by the current CETa scope.\n• Identify common components\, 
 symbols\, diagrams\, instruments\, and safety practices quickly and accura
 tely.\n• Choose the correct measurement/test method from a scenario.\n
 • Navigate mixed electronics questions without relying on one-topic-at-a
 -time cues.\n• Identify weak competency numbers and repair specific gaps
  instead of rereading everything.\n• Demonstrate readiness for full-leng
 th CETa practice work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks
  above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still
  cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do n
 ot count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list
  and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the g
 ap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the l
 earning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, 
 write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the n
 ext available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
