 0%2B%20Project%201%20Design\n• Assessment Center: https://numberclaw2.gi
 thub.io/alfred-university/assessments.html\n• Engineering Library: https
 ://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTI
 ON: Broad CETa general-electronics coverage plus mixed-domain troubleshoot
 ing.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete
  the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEE
 K 22 FOCUS: CETa Final Review II + Project 1Design\nETA/CETa SCOPE: All we
 ak rows from Practice #1\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Write Project 1 require
 ments\, architecture\, BOM\, pin map\, interface plan and repo while repai
 ring CETa misses.\n\nTHIS week's resources:\n- ETA CETa competencies: http
 s://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.
 etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n- ETA 6th Ed. Errata: https://www.etai.org/6
 thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Every misshas a written correction
  and fresh example\; Saturday: Book Practice Exam #2 under 2-hour limit. C
 ETa-ready only after ≥85%twice.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never co
 unts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> 
 document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recal
 l. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up ma
 rathon.\n\nTODAY:\nRepair Practice #1 misses with fresh examples. Draft Pr
 oject 1 requirements and acceptance criteria.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP TH
 ESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your sca
 nned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOF
 FICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Book Practice Exam 
 #2 pp.202–209 split across the Tuesday/Thursday review work\; repair mis
 ses by competency row.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Saturday: current official CETa pra
 ctice run #1 under a 2-hour limit. Target ≥85%.\nWHY: The second book ex
 am expands question exposure\; the current CETa practice remains the highe
 r-authority readiness check.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the pri
 mary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata co
 ntrol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER T
 ODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 22)\nBy the end of this event\, 
 you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Repair remaining CETa w
 eak areas using exact competency evidence.\n• Translate a real embedded 
 project idea into clear requirements and acceptance criteria.\n• Repair 
 any previously identified weak concept before treating it as mastered.\n\n
 COVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cov
 er every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonst
 rate one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as comp
 lete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked offici
 al or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION R
 ULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If
  you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on 
 a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block
 . No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
