 ring CETa misses.\n\nTHIS week's resources:\n- ETA CETa competencies: http
 s://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.
 etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n- ETA 6th Ed. Errata: https://www.etai.org/6
 thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Every misshas a written correction
  and fresh example\; Saturday: current official CETa practice run #1 under
  2-hour limit. Do not declare CETa-ready yet\; this is current CETa run #1
 . Target ≥85%.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -
 >retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start e
 ach non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a mi
 ssed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:
 \nTake a second full official practice run under the2-hour limit\, then ma
 p misses. CETa green light requires ≥85% on twofull runs\; otherwise con
 tinue weak-area repair.\n\nCETa PRACTICE READINESS GATE — ADVANCE/REPEAT
  DECISION: GREEN = mastery is demonstrable and you advance. YELLOW = advan
 ce but carry no more than 1–2 specific weak items forward with a short w
 ritten repair date. RED = a core/safety/practical gap is material\; use th
 e next available buffer/repair block before treating the gate as complete.
  The calendar date never overrides competence.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP T
 HESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your sc
 anned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOF
 FICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Book Practice Exam 
 #2 pp.202–209 split across the Tuesday/Thursday review work\; repair mis
 ses by competency row.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Saturday: current official CETa pra
 ctice run #1 under a 2-hour limit. Target ≥85%.\nWHY: The second book ex
 am expands question exposure\; the current CETa practice remains the highe
 r-authority readiness check.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the pri
 mary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata co
 ntrol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER T
 ODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 22)\nBy the end of this event\, 
 you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Repair remaining CETa w
 eak areas using exact competency evidence.\n• Translate a real embedded 
 project idea into clear requirements and acceptance criteria.\n• Create 
 a block diagram\, interface list\, pin map\, BOM\, and initial test plan.\
 n• Control Project 1 scope so it proves bridge-job skills without featur
 e creep.\n• Explain how each Project 1 feature maps to a readiness-check
 list skill.\n• Use current CETa practice performance to decide whether e
 xam readiness is green\, yellow\, or red.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned 
 resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome
  list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after
  the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a 
 short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource b
 efore closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work
 \, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demons
 trate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and rep
 air it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is r
 equired.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
