 ng-Up\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/lab
 s.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-univ
 ersity/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade hardware/firmwar
 e/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Di
 ve. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra d
 epth.\n\nWEEK 24 FOCUS: Project 1 Hardware Bring-Up\nETA/CETa SCOPE: Maint
 enance retrieval only\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Power\, GPIO\, button\, co
 ntrolled output\, UART\, clean wiring\, rail measurements/current draw.\n\
 nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU Developer Zone: https://www.st.com/co
 ntent/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n- ETA Common Formulas: http
 s://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Boardpowers safely\,
  core I/O and UART work\, measurements are documented\, and at least one b
 ring-up failure has a root-cause story.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone ne
 ver counts. Use learn -> retrieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> deb
 ug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced
  recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make
 -up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall from prior weeks. Stu
 dy this week’s scoped material and make a one-page memory summary. Compl
 ete8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content applies. School work takes
  priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\
 n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google
  Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-
 ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY
  GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.11 pp.85–90\, Ch
 .18 pp.159–164 and Ch.19 pp.165–175 during hardware bring-up.\nQUIZ / 
 REVIEW: No new book quiz\; cite the relevant page in your troubleshooting 
 notes when it informs a decision.\nWHY: Reuses CETa material as real engin
 eering-lab procedure instead of separating certification knowledge from jo
 b skill.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. 
 Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the o
 lder book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LE
 ARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 24)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able t
 o explain or demonstrate:\n• Perform safe first power-up using visual in
 spection\, continuity checks\, a current-limited supply\, and measured pow
 er rails.\n• Verify board power\, ground\, reset/boot conditions\, GPIO\
 , and UART before adding complexity.\n• Measure voltage/current and reco
 rd baseline current draw.\n• Use SWD/UART diagnostics to separate hardwa
 re\, firmware\, and configuration faults.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned 
 resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome
  list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after
  the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a 
 short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource b
 efore closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work
 \, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demons
 trate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and rep
 air it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is r
 equired.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
