SUMMARY:W25 • Project 1 Learn — Sensor & Interface Integration
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=25\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Sensor%20/%20I
 nterface%20Integration\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade
  hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career
  Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for 
 repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 25 FOCUS: Project 1 Sensor / Interface Inte
 gration\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5/13.x/8.x spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURP
 OSE: Integrate I2C/SPI sensor\, convert raw data to engineering units\, ca
 pture bus traffic and handle disconnect/address faults.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RES
 OURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial —SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/
 i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial —SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/
 serial-peripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Saleae support: https://support.sal
 eae.com/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Sensor/interface works end-to-end\, analyzer cap
 ture is interpretable\, and one physical or protocol fault is diagnosed an
 d documented.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->re
 trieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start each
  non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a misse
 d session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nF
 irst 10 min: spaced recall from prior weeks. Study this week’s scoped ma
 terial and make a one-page memory summary. Complete8–12 fresh CETa quest
 ions when ETA content applies. School work takes priority during exam-heav
 y weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CE
 T Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTE
 D page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.et
 ai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNM
 ENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.16 pp.144–147 and Ch.17 pp.149–155\; use
  current ETA + datasheets/tutorials for the actual I2C/SPI device.\nQUIZ /
  REVIEW: No new book quiz.\nWHY: Book architecture supports the concept\, 
 while the project proves modern interface implementation.\nSOURCE RULE: Th
 e 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wo
 rding + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omit
 s a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 25)
 \nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:
 \n• Integrate the chosen I2C/SPI sensor or peripheral into Project 1.\n
 • Read raw registers/data and convert values into meaningful engineering
  units.\n• Verify bus activity with a logic analyzer and correlate decod
 ed traffic with firmware behavior.\n• Handle missing device\, wrong addr
 ess/configuration\, timeout\, or invalid-data conditions.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDI
 T\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item
  in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of t
 hese items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write t
 he concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplem
 ental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish t
 he assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot e
 xplain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch
 -up list and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsh
 eet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
