 tual I2C/SPI device.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No new book quiz.\nWHY: Book architec
 ture supports the concept\, while the project proves modern interface impl
 ementation.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textboo
 k. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever th
 e older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED
  LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 25)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be abl
 e to explain or demonstrate:\n• Verify bus activity with a logic analyze
 r and correlate decoded traffic with firmware behavior.\n• Handle missin
 g device\, wrong address/configuration\, timeout\, or invalid-data conditi
 ons.\n• Confirm electrical interface requirements from the datasheet.\n
 • Document a working end-to-end peripheral path from hardware through fi
 rmware to observed output.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and t
 asks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you s
 till cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, 
 do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up 
 list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing t
 he gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check t
