DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=25\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Sensor%20/%20I
 nterface%20Integration\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfr
 ed-university/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade
  hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career
  Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for 
 repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 25 FOCUS: Project 1 Sensor / Interface Inte
 gration\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5/13.x/8.x spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURP
 OSE: Integrate I2C/SPI sensor\, convert raw data to engineering units\, ca
 pture bus traffic and handle disconnect/address faults.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RES
 OURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial —SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/
 i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial —SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/
 serial-peripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Saleae support: https://support.sal
 eae.com/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Sensor/interface works end-to-end\, analyzer cap
 ture is interpretable\, and one physical or protocol fault is diagnosed an
 d documented.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->re
 trieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start each
  non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a misse
 d session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY —
  ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Verify the sensor/peripheral datasheet pinout\, sup
 ply voltage\, logic levels\, bus address/mode\, and required pull-ups befo
 re wiring.\n2. Connect power\, ground\, and one interface at a time\; conf
 irm the device responds before adding application behavior.\n3. Read raw r
 egisters/data\, convert them to engineering units\, and compare the result
  with an expected or reference condition.\n4. Capture I²C/SPI or serial e
 vidence and test one failure case such as wrong address\, disconnected dev
 ice\, timeout\, or invalid response.\n5. Save the wiring/interface diagram
 \, configuration\, capture/log\, expected-versus-actual result\, and fault
  recovery in Project 1.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Offici
 al Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy
  and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata:
  https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — 
 V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.16 pp.144–147 and Ch.17 pp.
 149–155\; use current ETA + datasheets/tutorials for the actual I2C/SPI 
 device.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No new book quiz.\nWHY: Book architecture supports
  the concept\, while the project proves modern interface implementation.\n
 SOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ET
 A competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book 
 differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUT
 COMES (WEEK 25)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain 
 or demonstrate:\n• Integrate the chosen I2C/SPI sensor or peripheral int
 o Project 1.\n• Read raw registers/data and convert values into meaningf
 ul engineering units.\n• Verify bus activity with a logic analyzer and c
 orrelate decoded traffic with firmware behavior.\n• Handle missing devic
 e\, wrong address/configuration\, timeout\, or invalid-data conditions.\n
 • Confirm electrical interface requirements from the datasheet.\n• Doc
 ument a working end-to-end peripheral path from hardware through firmware 
 to observed output.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks ab
 ove are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still ca
 nnot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not 
 count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list an
 d use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.
 \n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the lear
 ning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, wri
 te that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next
  available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
