DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=26\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Firmware%20Arc
 hitecture\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-u
 niversity/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade hardware/firm
 ware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep
  Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extr
 a depth.\n\nWEEK 26 FOCUS: Project 1 Firmware Architecture\nETA/CETa SCOPE
 : 13.10–13.12 spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Timers\, interrupt
 s\, PWM\, nonblocking FSM\, timeouts\, error codes and diagnostic output.\
 n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU Developer Zone: https://www.st.com/
 content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Firmware 
 runs without long blocking delays\, timing is measured\, error paths are e
 xercised\, and architecture can be explained at interview depth.\n\nSYSTEM
  RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/co
 de -> build/measure -> debug ->document. Start each non-exam study block w
 ith ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justificat
 ion for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced rec
 all from priorweeks. Study this week’s scoped material and make a one-pa
 ge memory summary. Complete 8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content a
 pplies. School work takes priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE H
 UB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.
 : use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK 
 ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSh
 eet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Refere
 nce Ch.17 pp.151–155 and Ch.16 logic/sequential sections pp.136–143.\n
 QUIZ / REVIEW: Explain your firmware state machine and hardware-control fl
 ow without the book open.\nWHY: Connects book control/programming concepts
  to structured embedded firmware.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is th
 e primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA erra
 ta control whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAF
 TER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 26)\nBy the end of this eve
 nt\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Organize Project 1
  firmware into understandable modules with clear responsibilities.\n• Us
 e a nonblocking finite-state machine for system behavior.\n• Use timers/
 interrupts where appropriate without creating timing-dependent chaos.\n•
  Implement timeouts\, error states\, diagnostic messages\, and recoverable
  fault handling.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above
  are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still canno
 t explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not cou
 nt that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and u
 se the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\
 nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learnin
 g outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write 
 that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next av
 ailable review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
