DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=26\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Firmware%20Arc
 hitecture\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-u
 niversity/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade hardware/firm
 ware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep
  Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extr
 a depth.\n\nWEEK 26 FOCUS: Project 1 Firmware Architecture\nETA/CETa SCOPE
 : 13.10–13.12 spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Timers\, interrupt
 s\, PWM\, nonblocking FSM\, timeouts\, error codes and diagnostic output.\
 n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU Developer Zone: https://www.st.com/
 content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Firmware 
 runs without long blocking delays\, timing is measured\, error paths are e
 xercised\, and architecture can be explained at interview depth.\n\nSYSTEM
  RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/co
 de -> build/measure -> debug ->document. Start each non-exam study block w
 ith ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justificat
 ion for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nApply the topic in code\
 , simulation\, schematic analysis or troubleshooting. Predict expected beh
 avior before running/measuring. Record one failure or misconception and it
 s correction.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associa
 te CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the P
 RINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://w
 ww.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK AS
 SIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.17 pp.151–155 and Ch.16 logic/sequent
 ial sections pp.136–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Explain your firmware state mac
 hine and hardware-control flow without the book open.\nWHY: Connects book 
 control/programming concepts to structured embedded firmware.\nSOURCE RULE
 : The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competenc
 y wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or 
 omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK
  26)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstr
 ate:\n• Use timers/interrupts where appropriate without creating timing-
 dependent chaos.\n• Implement timeouts\, error states\, diagnostic messa
 ges\, and recoverable fault handling.\n• Use const/volatile/bit operatio
 ns appropriately in hardware-facing code.\n• Debug firmware systematical
 ly and explain the architecture without relying on generated code alone.\n
 \nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to c
 over every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demon
 strate one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as co
 mplete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked offi
 cial or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION
  RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. 
 If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept o
 n a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review blo
 ck. No spreadsheet logging is required.
