SUMMARY:W26 • Project 1 Lab — Firmware Integration & Test
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=26\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Firmware%20Arc
 hitecture\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university
 /labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-
 university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade hardware/fir
 mware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Dee
 p Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or ext
 ra depth.\n\nWEEK 26 FOCUS: Project 1 Firmware Architecture\nETA/CETa SCOP
 E: 13.10–13.12 spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Timers\, interrup
 ts\, PWM\, nonblocking FSM\, timeouts\, error codes and diagnostic output.
 \n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU Developer Zone: https://www.st.com
 /content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\n\nMASTERY GATE: Firmware
  runs without long blocking delays\, timing is measured\, error paths are 
 exercised\, and architecture can be explained at interview depth.\n\nSYSTE
 M RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/c
 ode -> build/measure -> debug ->document. Start each non-exam study block 
 with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justifica
 tion for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1.
  Identify each firmware module\, its responsibility\, and the system state
 s/transitions before running the integrated build.\n2. Verify nonblocking 
 timing\, inputs\, outputs\, serial diagnostics\, and normal state transiti
 ons.\n3. Test timeout/error behavior by disconnecting or delaying one depe
 ndency\; confirm the system enters a known error state and can recover saf
 ely.\n4. Use debugger\, serial log\, scope\, or logic-analyzer evidence to
  isolate and correct one integration fault.\n5. Save the state diagram\, m
 odule map\, build/version information\, test cases\, diagnostic evidence\,
  and verified fix.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official As
 sociate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and 
 the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: http
 s://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BO
 OK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.17 pp.151–155 and Ch.16 logic/se
 quential sections pp.136–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Explain your firmware stat
 e machine and hardware-control flow without the book open.\nWHY: Connects 
 book control/programming concepts to structured embedded firmware.\nSOURCE
  RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA comp
 etency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differ
 s or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES 
 (WEEK 26)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or dem
 onstrate:\n• Organize Project 1 firmware into understandable modules wit
 h clear responsibilities.\n• Use a nonblocking finite-state machine for 
 system behavior.\n• Use timers/interrupts where appropriate without crea
 ting timing-dependent chaos.\n• Implement timeouts\, error states\, diag
 nostic messages\, and recoverable fault handling.\n• Use const/volatile/
 bit operations appropriately in hardware-facing code.\n• Debug firmware 
 systematically and explain the architecture without relying on generated c
 ode alone.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are i
 ntended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot expl
 ain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count tha
 t item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the
  linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-
 END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point for the wee
 k. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on real hardware/
 code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COM
 PLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes 
 below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one co
 ncept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available rev
 iew block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
