 adiness scorecard.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- GitHub Skills — Introduc
 tion to GitHub: https://github.com/skills/introduction-to-github\n\nMASTER
 Y GATE: Common core + Project 1 + one role add-on demonstrable\; portfolio
  and resume-defensible\; 90-sec transition story\, 2-min project overview 
 and 5-min technical deep dive ready.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never
  counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug
  ->document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced re
 call. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up
  marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nBuild\, measure\, debug and document the week’s de
 liverable. Update Git/project evidence. Stop at the scheduled end\; do not
  compensate for a missed session with a marathon.\n\nBRIDGE-JOB APPLICATIO
 N GATE — ADVANCE/REPEAT DECISION: GREEN = mastery is demonstrable and yo
 u advance. YELLOW = advance but carry no more than 1–2 specific weak ite
 ms forward with a short written repair date. RED = a core/safety/practical
  gap is material\; use the next available buffer/repair block before treat
 ing the gate as complete. The calendar date never overrides competence.\n\
 nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Gui
 de\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numb
 ers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thE
 dASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD /
  USE: Reference Ch.21 pp.182–187 + Ch.22 pp.188–193.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: N
 o exam-style quiz\; convert these chapters into polished resume bullets\, 
