 essionalism and technical-writing material directly strengthens the applic
 ation package.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa text
 book. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever
  the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUI
 RED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 30)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be 
 able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Present Project 1 as an employer-faci
 ng engineering artifact rather than a hobby build.\n• Write truthful\, r
 ole-specific resume bullets for R&D electronics\, hardware test/validation
 \, and integration roles.\n• Organize GitHub/portfolio evidence so a rev
 iewer can understand the problem\, design\, measurements\, failures\, and 
 results quickly.\n• Deliver a clear 90-second career-transition story an
 d a 2-minute/5-minute Project 1 explanation.\n• Defend your own C\, Pyth
 on\, electronics\, instruments\, protocols\, and troubleshooting decisions
  in interview questions.\n• Apply the bridge-job green-light criteria: p
 ermanent/full-time\, acceptable compensation/benefits\, school-compatible\
 , and genuinely hardware/electronics relevant.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assi
 gned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this ou
 tcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items 
 after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept 
 on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resou
 rce before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned
  work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or d
 emonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list an
 d repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging
