SUMMARY:W31 • Application Sprint 1 — Targeted Electronics / Embedded Ro
 les
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN T
 HESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.io/al
 fred-university/week.html?week=31\n• Search this topic: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Application%20Sprint%20%2B%2
 0Interview%20Feedback%20Loop\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2
 .github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-
 grade hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → C
 areer Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive
  for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 31 FOCUS: APPLICATION SPRINT + Intervi
 ew Feedback Loop\nETA/CETa SCOPE: No new CETa content\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PUR
 POSE: Begin permanent full-time bridge-job applications\; track requested 
 skills\, interview questions and gaps\; keep school-compatible job filter.
 \n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Use the project/readiness resources already 
 in your guide.\n\nMASTERY GATE: Apply only to genuine electronics/hardware
 /R&D/test roles\; use market feedback to improveweak skills without delayi
 ng applications for optional perfection.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone n
 ever counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> de
 bug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of space
 d recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy mak
 e-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nApply to a focused batch of permanent full-time 
 hardware/test/R&D roles. Track role family\, salary\, schedule\, skills an
 d outcome.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate 
 CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRIN
 TED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.
 etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIG
 NMENT\nREAD / USE: No new book reading. Use Ch.21/22 only when application
  feedback exposes a communication/documentation weakness.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: 
 None.\nWHY: Application week should be execution-focused\; the book become
 s a targeted reference rather than another task.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edi
 tion book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + c
 urrent ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a curre
 nt topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 31)\nBy the 
 end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Pra
 ctice technical and behavioral interviews using real project/troubleshooti
 ng stories.\n• Track interview misses and convert them into dated learni
 ng repairs.\n• Maintain the portfolio while applying without restarting 
 the entire curriculum.\n• Use market feedback to refine role targeting w
 hile preserving the embedded-systems trajectory.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe as
 signed resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this 
 outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these item
 s after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concep
 t on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental res
 ource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assign
 ed work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or
  demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list 
 and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet loggi
 ng is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
